&lt;p&gt;Product Marketing Manager I Viator&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tripadvisor&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Tripadvisor Group connects people to experiences worth sharing, and aims to be the world’s most trusted source for travel and experiences. We leverage our brands, technology, and capabilities to connect our global audience with partners through rich content, travel guidance, and two-sided marketplaces for experiences, accommodations, restaurants, and other travel categories. The subsidiaries of Tripadvisor, Inc. (Nasdaq: TRIP), include a portfolio of travel brands and businesses, including Tripadvisor, Viator, and TheFork.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;This role owns key aspects of commercial strategy, go-to-market, and narrative for how Viator grows value across its supply organisation — shaping strategy alongside Commercial and Product teams, not just executing it, and turning that strategy into positioning and enablement that suppliers understand, trust, and act on. It sits at the intersection of commercial strategy, product, and supplier-facing marketing, and is accountable for making sure Viator&#39;s most important supply-side initiatives are right, and that they land with operators, not just internally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The strength of any supply-side initiative starts with whether the strategy behind it is right — and that requires someone close enough to the evidence to shape it, not just market it after the fact. This role brings senior commercial marketing capability that can build strategy, ground it in original research, and carry it through to execution that lands with operators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Job Location: Hybrid&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is a hybrid position in London, UK. Travel to company offices is expected 1-2 days per week.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Build strategy and identify key initiatives to enable us to meet our company goals - bringing a point of view on what Viator should do next and why, backed by evidence rather than assumption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Independent Research &amp;amp; Insight:&lt;/strong&gt; Run research into supplier behaviour, needs, and market dynamics - designing and conducting the work directly rather than relying solely on other teams&#39; output and use it to shape strategy before it&#39;s built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Roadmap Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; Work as a key partner with product, using supplier insight and data to actively guide what gets built and prioritised.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial GTM Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Take supply-side commercial strategy such as pricing, promotions, incentive structures, new programs and turn it into positioning and launch plans that suppliers act on, from first announcement through adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supplier Growth Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Commercial teams to translate operator insight into marketing and product initiatives that measurably grow supplier earnings and engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lifecycle &amp;amp; CRM Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Shape supplier lifecycle CRM programs so that engagement, retention, and reactivation efforts stay aligned to what&#39;s commercially important right now.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initiative Launch &amp;amp; Rollout:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the end-to-end rollout of major supply-side initiatives - sequencing, localisation where relevant, and adapting positioning and enablement to what actually works for the operators it&#39;s aimed at, rather than exporting a single playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive &amp;amp; Market Intelligence:&lt;/strong&gt; Track how competitors win and retain supply, and turn that into a sharper Viator offering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Skills and Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in product marketing, with experience owning commercial or GTM strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing product roadmap as a peer to product teams, backed by evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grasp of two-sided marketplace dynamics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working directly with data science/analytics and core metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sharp GTM and positioning craft — turns ambiguous strategy into messaging people act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across more than one stage of a supplier/partner lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation packages (routinely benchmarked against the latest industry data), including base salary and annual bonuses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;“Work your way” with flexibility to suit your lifestyle. Tripadvisor Group takes a remote-friendly approach to collaboration across a worldwide team, with the option to join on-site as often as you’d like or as required by your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible schedule. Work-life balance is ingrained in our culture by design. Trust and accountability make it work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Donation matching. Give back? Give more! We match qualifying charitable donations annually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition assistance. Want to level up your career? We love to hear it! Receive annual support for qualified programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifestyle benefit. An annual benefit to spend on yourself. Use it on travel, wellness, or whatever suits you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel perks. We believe that travel is employee development, so we provide discounts and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee assistance program. We’re here for you with resources and programs to help you through life’s challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health benefits. We offer great coverage and competitive premiums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous referral scheme. Help us grow and be rewarded with generous awards for referring successful candidates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Cultural Pillars:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Traveler first&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We exist to create value for our customer, the traveler. We enable our suppliers and partners to unlock this value. Their collective behaviors and insights are what drives us.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execution is our edge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We act fast, experiment, learn from failure, iterate, and improve the solutions of tomorrow across every aspect of our business. Our execution is agile, data-driven, prioritised, and built to scale. We assume no problem is someone else’s problem and finish what can be done today, knowing tomorrow will bring fresh challenges.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We succeed together&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The best outcomes are driven by empathic, humble, and diverse subject matter experts working toward shared goals. We collaborate relentlessly, challenge assumptions, give actionable feedback, and set each other up for success through empowered teams with a clear charter. We transparently take ownership of our growth, individually and as a team. We celebrate the quality of our effort, our learnings, and our collective achievements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to create an accessible and inclusive experience for all candidates. If you need a reasonable accommodation during the application or the recruiting process, please make sure to reach out to your individual recruiter or our team at AccessibleRecruiting@tripadvisor.com.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have any additional questions about careers at Tripadvisor you can email us at recruitment@tripadvisor.com. We have all the answers!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join our Movement and Champion Restaurant Culture! 💚&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At TheFork we believe that the best things in life happen around the table.&lt;br&gt;As the leading restaurant booking platform in Europe, we connect the broadest community of loyal diners with the world’s favorite restaurants. Powered by innovation and a deep passion for the restaurant industry, we create unique dining experiences across 11 countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re part of the Tripadvisor Group and proud to be building a diverse, people-first culture where “respect”, “ownership”, “growth” and “better together” values thrive.&lt;br&gt;If you’re passionate about food, technology, and making a real impact, your seat at the table is ready.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;👉&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.careers.thefork.com/&quot;&gt; Discover life at TheFork&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;QA Automation Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, you will join our Engineering organization within a dedicated Quality Engineering team of around 10 passionate engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you won&#39;t just write test scripts—you will build the platform, tooling, and infrastructure that power quality across all our engineering squads. You’ll be working in a truly international environment, collaborating daily with talented developers and engineers across Western and Eastern Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a strong software development background and love building tools that make other engineers faster and more efficient, this is the place for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build tools, not just tests:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Design, build, and scale state-of-the-art test automation frameworks and internal tooling (our core stack: Playwright + TypeScript).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the ecosystem:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Act as the technical architect for our entire test ecosystem—owning repositories, design patterns, and long-term codebase health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empower the engineering org:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Enable developers to write fast, reliable tests by providing clean abstractions, SDKs, utility libraries, and reusable components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape test architecture:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Drive key engineering decisions around test layering, fixture design, data isolation, and environment stability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve system testability:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Partner with feature teams to architect highly testable APIs, frontends, and data pipelines—without having to write their feature tests for them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Master CI/CD &amp;amp; Performance:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Own and optimize modern test pipelines (Jenkins), ruthlessly cutting down execution times and eliminating flakiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solve systemic problems:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Hunt down root causes of instability and slow feedback loops to implement permanent structural fixes rather than quick patches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovate with AI:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Experiment with and integrate AI-driven testing tools and LLMs to push our testing capabilities and developer productivity forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elevate engineering standards:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Mentor engineers, define quality gates/metrics, and champion a modern Quality Engineering culture across the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2 to 5 years of hands-on experience as a Software Development Engineer in Test (SDET) or Quality Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;with a strong focus on tooling, infrastructure, and framework design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solid Software Engineering background:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Whether you started as a Software Developer or built a strong coding foundation in QA, you write clean, scalable, and maintainable code (TypeScript / JavaScript experience required).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Framework expertise:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Proven experience designing and architecting automation frameworks from scratch or at scale, ideally using Playwright.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep architectural understanding:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Mastery of test design patterns, the test pyramid, data management strategies, and test isolation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CI/CD mastery:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Strong experience configuring and optimizing CI/CD pipelines (e.g., Jenkins) with an obsession for fast feedback loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;API &amp;amp; Systems knowledge:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Comfortable testing REST and GraphQL interfaces and designing reusable API client layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer Advocate mindset:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Passionate about cross-team collaboration, technical mentorship, and making developers&#39; lives easier.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent in English (written and spoken)&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to collaborate effectively in an international environment across Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
